        "title": "Ring announces its first smart lock, solving a major pain point for smart home users",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/07/ring-announces-first-ever-smart-lock-solving-core-problem/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/10/Ring-smart-lock.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Today, Amazon’s Ring subsidiary is announcing its first ever smart lock. It solves a key problem that looms over many smart lock owners: dead batteries. Ring has a clever solution to negate that problem, and it’ll be available in Q1 2027. Additionally, the company is announcing a few new security cameras with improved low-light performance.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"ring,smart-home\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1073059\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/07/ring-announces-first-ever-smart-lock-solving-core-problem/#more-1073059\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
