        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/05/openai-details-new-text-watermarking-system-for-chatgpt-codex-and-the-api/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/04/chatgpt-red.webp?w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">OpenAI today announced how it will comply with the EU AI Act, which requires providers of generative AI systems to mark AI-generated text in a way that makes it identifiable. Here are the details.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"chatgpt,codex,openai\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1072778\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/05/openai-details-new-text-watermarking-system-for-chatgpt-codex-and-the-api/#more-1072778\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
